  "generic_lessons": [
    "Treat native getter parameters as strict API contracts; a production hash is not a unit row index, even when both are numbers. Reuse the actual qualified consumer before native execution.",
    "Partial diagnostic output before a timeout may support narrow facts but never replaces a terminal command acknowledgement for the whole probe.",
    "A native exception after an owner diagnostic error must be retained and attributed carefully; do not blame a model or product implementation without independent causal evidence.",
    "An empty state that reappears after reload may have been reinitialized. Persist a distinguishable intent/token and inspect the actual restored state before crediting serialization.",
    "Void-returning native commands can succeed. A transparent observer must preserve nil holes, all returns and original exception objects, and keep its own save errors from changing the command behavior.",
